Source-Makefile: package/network/services/p910nd/Makefile

Package: p910nd
Submenu: Printing
Version: 0.97-9
Depends: +libc 
Conflicts: 
Menu-Depends: 
Provides: 
Section: net
Category: Network
Repository: base
Title: A small non-spooling printer server
Maintainer: Philipp Kerling <pkerling@casix.org>
Require-User: p910nd=393:lp=7
Source: p910nd-0.97.tar.bz2
License: GPLv2
LicenseFiles: COPYING
Type: ipkg
Description:  p910nd is a small daemon that copies any data received on
 the port it is listening on to the corresponding printer
 port. It is primarily intended for diskless Linux hosts
 running as printer drivers but there is no reason why it
 could not be used on diskful hosts. Port 9100 is copied
 to /dev/lp0, 9101 to /dev/lp1 and 9102 to /dev/lp2. The
 default is port 9100 to /dev/lp0.
http://p910nd.sourceforge.net
Philipp Kerling <pkerling@casix.org>
@@


